course: dictionary
lesson: 3342
title: Ex: a small word with three jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word ex can do different jobs. Look at the words around it to see which one it is doing. At the start of a word, ex- is a prefix, a little piece added to the front that changes the meaning. «Our ex-teacher now lives by the sea.» Ex- here means former: she used to be a teacher, but she is not one now.
explain: «Prices are shown ex VAT.» Here ex means without: the price does not include the tax. In maths, the letter x (said «ex») is often a number we do not know yet. The sentence or the sum around it tells you which job ex is doing.
explain: A good check is to swap in a simple meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense. Does «our former teacher» fit? Yes, so ex- means former. Does «without VAT» fit? Yes, so ex means without. Context helps you choose.
fact: A prefix is a few letters added to the front of a word to change its meaning.
fact: «Ex-» means former or no longer, as in «ex-president» or «ex-pupil».
fact: An ex-pupil is someone who used to be a pupil at a school, but is not one now.
fact: «Ex VAT» means without the tax, so the tax is not included in the price.
fact: In maths, x (said «ex») is often a letter standing for a number we do not know yet.
exercise: «Our ex-teacher now lives by the sea.» What does ex- mean here? | Learning to be a teacher | Still teaching at the same school | *Former, no longer a teacher
exercise: «Prices are shown ex VAT, so the tax is not included.» What does ex mean in this sentence? | Before | *Without | Very expensive | Extra
exercise: In the sum x + 4 = 10, what does the letter x (said «ex») stand for? | 14 | 40 | *6 | 4
test: «The ex-president gave a speech at our school.» What does ex- tell you about the president? | He will become president next year | *He is no longer president | He is the best president ever
test: «The shop sells the book ex VAT.» What does ex mean in this sentence? | Free | Very cheap | *Without the tax
exam: Which sentence uses ex- to mean former? | Please pay ex VAT for the tickets | *Our ex-head teacher now runs a chess club | The sum needs x to be 5
